  "whyNotPopulation": "We divide by the size of each Wikipedia, not by population. Malaysia has roughly a fifth of Indonesia's people but the Malay edition draws roughly a fifth of the Indonesian edition's reads, so the two cancel less than they look like they should. What is left is a difference in what gets read, not how many can read.",
